id: pm-rtn5h6
title: "Defect-escape ratchet: every escaped defect must land a gate that would have caught it, tracked as evidence on the fixing item"
description: Establish a defect-escape ratchet in which every escaped defect contributes a durable negative control and a repository-owned gate that would have prevented recurrence.
type: Task
status: open
priority: 1
tags[6]: ci,continuous-improvement,defect-detection,governance,process,quality-gate
created_at: "2026-07-24T23:46:03.890Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-29T21:22:24.534Z"
author: maintainer-agent
estimated_minutes: 720
acceptance_criteria: "A defined escape class taxonomy covers at minimum: production defect, nightly regression, scanner finding, and review-caught-late; Items of an escape class carry a structured gate-evidence field naming the gate added or strengthened, or a reviewed no-gate waiver; A governance check reports escaped-defect items closed without gate evidence, mapped to an owning item like every other warning; A periodic report shows escapes per class over time and the gates added, so the ratchet is visible rather than asserted"
goal: ci-detects-every-defect
objective: "The pipeline strictly improves: no defect class escapes twice"
value: "The pipeline currently improves by intuition. Escapes are fixed, but nothing forces the question of which gate should have caught it, so the same class escapes again in a different file."
impact: "Turns every production defect, nightly red, and scanner finding into a permanent, compounding increase in detection capability."
outcome: "Closing an item that fixes an escaped defect requires naming the gate that now covers it, or recording an explicit no-gate-possible waiver; the ratio is reportable over time."
why_now: "The workspace already records the raw material — resolution fields, close reasons, linked tests, and history — so the policy can be enforced with the governance surface that exists rather than new infrastructure."
parent: pm-u9d0
risk: low
confidence: high
