  pm-u9d0,implements,"2026-07-26T05:55:43.796Z"
body: "## Problem\nThis repository has a deep gate stack — coverage, static quality, complexity, contracts snapshot, changelog drift, boundary ratchet, five external analyzers, nightly matrix. Despite that, defects still escape to nightly and to users, and the recurring pattern in the history is a class of defect that escapes, gets fixed at one site, and then escapes again at a second site months later.\n\n## Approach\nMake the gate the deliverable, not the fix. Every escape closes with a named gate. Class-level fixes are already the informal norm in this workspace; this makes the norm checkable.\n\n## Precedent in the history\nRepeated multi-site classes — path canonicalization asymmetry, POSIX-only assertions in specs, silent-zero filter validation, capability-blind hint rendering — each escaped two or more times before a class-level fix landed. Every one of them would have been caught once by a gate written at first escape.\n\n## Boundary\nNot blame attribution. Not a mandatory postmortem document. One structured field and one governance check."
